
# The Pages workflow checks the codecave.pro repo out here for its build
# toolchain. CI-only, but ignored so a local reproduction of the workflow does
# not offer to commit someone else's repository.
/_toolchain/

# ds-bundle/ is the design-sync upload staging directory, and it is HALF derived
# and half authored — so it is half ignored. The old blanket `ds-bundle/` rule
# called the whole thing "regenerated; not a source artifact", which was true of
# 500K of it and false of the other 32K.
#
# DERIVED — ignored. Every one of these is a byte-for-byte copy of a tracked
# file under docs/, materialized by docs/tools/build-ds-bundle.sh. Tracking them
# would mean every palette or font change needs a second, forgettable commit,
# and would put a duplicate 500K of Satoshi binaries in the history.
ds-bundle/colors_and_type.css
ds-bundle/tokens/
ds-bundle/fonts/

# AUTHORED — tracked, and deliberately not listed here: README.md, styles.css,
# guidelines/brand.md, and components/Foundations/*/*.html. Those seven files
# exist nowhere else in this repo and nothing regenerates them. Under the old
# blanket rule they were untracked source: invisible to review and one `rm -rf`
# from gone.

# Internal planning, kept on disk and out of the published repository. Jira is
# the system of record for open work. TODO.md was the staging area in front of
# it and is now gone — its six items were filed as CCWEB2-314..317 (label
# `brand-kit`) or closed out, and CLAUDE.md carries the index so an empty repo
# is never mistaken for an empty backlog. ASTRO-MIGRATION.md survives only as a
# local working copy; its substance is CCWEB2-317.
#
# WEBSITE-REVIEW.md is NOT here on purpose: twelve places cite it, three of them
# comments inside the shipped colors_and_type.css, and README.md opens with a
# promise about it. It goes only when those citations point at Jira instead.
/TODO.md
/ASTRO-MIGRATION.md

# The npm package (CCWEB2-318). packages/brand/ is a PURE DERIVATIVE of docs/:
# every byte it publishes is copied or compiled from there, so none of its
# output is source and none of it is tracked. `npm run check` asserts the
# derivation still holds; package-lock.json IS tracked, because a lockfile is
# the only thing making the build reproducible.
node_modules/
packages/*/dist/
packages/*/.tmp/
